# Offsite backup destination for backup.sh (RM_OFFSITE_REMOTE).
#
# Empty means local-only backups: a host that loses its disk loses the backups with it, which
# satisfies nothing in the RPO/RTO targets (requirements §11, AC-16). backup.sh checks whether the
# named remote exists and skips the offsite sync when it does not, so this file being a template
# is a silent downgrade rather than an error — decide the destination and fill it in.
#
# Example for an S3-compatible bucket (Backblaze B2, Wasabi, another region's Spaces):
#
# [offsite]
# type = s3
# provider = Other
# access_key_id = <key>
# secret_access_key = <secret>
# endpoint = <endpoint>
# acl = private
#
# Then set RM_OFFSITE_REMOTE=offsite:research-management in infra/.env.
